<GuidePageShell
  slug="when-do-puppies-stop-growing"
  title="When Do Puppies Stop Growing? By Breed Size"
  description="Growth timelines by breed size, what affects adult weight, and when to switch from puppy to adult food."
  answer="Most puppies stop growing taller between 9 and 18 months depending on breed size: toy breeds finish earliest, around 9 to 10 months, while giant breeds can keep growing for 18 to 24 months. Weight and muscle often keep filling out for months after height stops."
  takeaways={[
    'Toy and small breeds reach adult size at about 9–12 months.',
    'Large and giant breeds can take 15–24 months.',
